Subject: [PATCH] audio: Force MTK HAL to API version 2.0

MediaTek's Android 6.0 audio HAL claims to support API version 3.0,
but it has an inverted ABI structure for audio_port_config_device_ext
and audio_port_config_mix_ext compared to standard AOSP.

This mismatch causes the AudioPolicyManager to pass incorrect values
(like device.type 0) to createAudioPatch, resulting in a -22 (Invalid 
argument) failure and completely breaking wired headset routing.

By forcing the HAL version down to 2.0, we bypass createAudioPatch 
and force the APM to use the legacy setParameters("connect=4") method, 
which works perfectly.

Change-Id: I1234567890abcdef1234567890abcdef12345678
---
 audio/2.0/default/Device.cpp | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/audio/2.0/default/Device.cpp b/audio/2.0/default/Device.cpp
index abcdef1..1234567 100644
--- a/audio/2.0/default/Device.cpp
+++ b/audio/2.0/default/Device.cpp
@@ -34,7 +34,14 @@ namespace implementation {
 
 Device::Device(audio_hw_device_t* device)
         : mDevice(device) {
+
+    // MTK Android 6.0 Workaround: Downgrade HAL version to 2.0 
+    // to bypass broken createAudioPatch ABI.
+    if (mDevice->common.version >= AUDIO_DEVICE_API_VERSION_3_0) {
+        ALOGI("Forcing audio HAL version to 2.0 for MTK workaround");
+        mDevice->common.version = AUDIO_DEVICE_API_VERSION_2_0;
+    }
 }
 
 Device::~Device() {
